Remove Only Starting and Ending Commas in Power Automate
If you want to remove only the first comma at the start and the last comma at the end (but preserve any commas in between), here's the cleanest solution:

Method 1: Using Conditional Expressions
if(
  startsWith(variables('YourStringVariable'), ','),
  substring(variables('YourStringVariable'), 1, length(variables('YourStringVariable'))),
  variables('YourStringVariable')
)
Then for the trailing comma:

if(
  endsWith(variables('ResultFromAbove'), ','),
  substring(variables('ResultFromAbove'), 0, sub(length(variables('ResultFromAbove')), 1)),
  variables('ResultFromAbove')
)
Method 2: Combined in a Single Expression
if(
  endsWith(
    if(
      startsWith(variables('YourStringVariable'), ','),
      substring(variables('YourStringVariable'), 1, length(variables('YourStringVariable'))),
      variables('YourStringVariable')
    ),
  ','),
  substring(
    if(
      startsWith(variables('YourStringVariable'), ','),
      substring(variables('YourStringVariable'), 1, length(variables('YourStringVariable'))),
      variables('YourStringVariable')
    ),
    0,
    sub(length(
      if(
        startsWith(variables('YourStringVariable'), ','),
        substring(variables('YourStringVariable'), 1, length(variables('YourStringVariable'))),
        variables('YourStringVariable')
      )
    ), 1)
  ),
  if(
    startsWith(variables('YourStringVariable'), ','),
    substring(variables('YourStringVariable'), 1, length(variables('YourStringVariable'))),
    variables('YourStringVariable')
  )
)
Method 3: Simplified Using Variables (Recommended)
First action: Remove starting comma

if(startsWith(variables('InputString'), ','), 
   substring(variables('InputString'), 1, length(variables('InputString'))), 
   variables('InputString'))
→ Store in variable TempString

Second action: Remove ending comma

if(endsWith(variables('TempString'), ','), 
   substring(variables('TempString'), 0, sub(length(variables('TempString')), 1)), 
   variables('TempString'))
Examples:
Input: ",test" → Output: "test"

Input: "test," → Output: "test"

Input: ",test,test," → Output: "test,test"

Input: "test" → Output: "test" (unchanged)

Input: ",test,test" → Output: "test,test"

Input: "test,test," → Output: "test,test"

This approach ensures only the very first and very last commas are removed, while preserving all commas within the string.
